{"raw": {"https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/8382": {"title": "Office of Human Resources1201 Locust Avenue, Fairmont, West Virginia 26554", "description": "Fairmont State University Portal | Campus Police Officer Skip to Main Content Office of Human Resources 1201 Locust Avenue, Fairmont, West Virginia 26554 Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Campus Police Officer Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Summary Working Title Campus Police Officer Type of Position Staff - Full Time Department Pooled Staff Position Appointment Length July - June (12 mo) Benefits Eligible? Yes Published Salary Requested Part-Time Staff Hours NA F.T.E. 1.00 Grant Funded Position? No If temporary (or grant funded) position, indicate ending date Description of Job Duties and Responsibilities Supports Fairmont State University by establishing and maintaining a safe atmosphere for the faculty, staff, students, and visitors by providing police and security services. Patrols campus in vehicle and on foot daily and during special events. Enforces all laws, regulations, and policies as needed. Works independently on a day-to-day basis under the supervision of a supervisor, but with the ability to deal with unusual situations as needed. General duties and responsibilities include but are not limited to: Serves as a preliminary and follow-up investigator; Patrols campus checking buildings and infrastructure for security issues and deficiencies which make the institution vulnerable to criminal acts; Patrols during special events, such as athletic events, concerts, etc. Directs traffic before, during and after the events; Provides crowd control which can include managing large numbers of people; Enforces all Federal, State, and Local laws, ordinances, and University regulations and policies; Enforces campus parking and traffic regulations; Makes arrests in accordance with departmental policies; Investigates traffic-related and general complaints; Testifies in court as needed; Watches for hazards and other dangerous or damaging situations; Administers first aid and provides or arranges necessary transportation; Provides police escorts as needed to protect property or people; Assists with the Fairmont State University Police Academy as needed; and Performs related duties as assigned or as directed. Minimum Required Education High School diploma or G.E.D. certificate Required Licenses and/or Certifications Valid WV Driver\u2019s License Minimum Required Qualifications No experience or up to 6 months of experience; however, any equivalent combination of education and/or experience is acceptable which provides an applicant the listed knowledge, skills, and abilities and the capacity to perform the essential functions of the job. Preferred Qualifications West Virginia Law Enforcement Officer certification preferred, but not required Associate or Bachelor degree in Criminal Justice Enroll in a Police Academy program upon hiring Posting Detail Information Requisition Number 2026003SP Number of Vacancies Pooled Position Anticipated Hire Date Varies Position End Date (if temporary) Job Open Date 06/19/2025 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Advertising Summary Quicklink for Posting https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/8381 Job Duties Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Optional Documents Certification/License Transcript #1 Transcript #2 Transcript #3 Contact Us For questions relating to Faculty/Staff positions, please e-mail the Human Resources Office at HR@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4111. For questions relating to Student Employment, please e-mail the Student Employment Office at studentjobs@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4836. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11677": {"title": "Instructor of Nursing", "description": "Fairmont State University Portal | Instructor of Nursing Skip to Main Content Office of Human Resources 1201 Locust Avenue, Fairmont, West Virginia 26554 Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Instructor of Nursing Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Summary Working Title Instructor of Nursing Type of Position Faculty Department College of Nursing Appointment Length Aug - May (9 mo) Tenure Status 3 - Faculty, not tenure eligible Academic Rank 4 - Instructor Is this considered a \"term\" position? No Benefits Eligible? Yes Published Salary F.T.E. 1.00 Grant Funded Position? No If temporary (or grant funded) position, indicate ending date Description of Job Duties and Responsibilities Teaching: Participates in the development and evaluation of the ASN and/or BSN program Develops, teaches, and evaluates assigned courses Evaluates student performance on exams and course assignments Evaluates student performance in the clinical environment; including skills lab and simulation lab Assumes responsibility for serving as a course coordinator, as appropriate Coordinates clinical rotation with clinical agency and clinical adjuncts Teaches 12 credits per semester, includes theory, clinical, skills lab and simulation lab Participate in ongoing course and curriculum revision Service: Provides engaged service at the programmatic, School, University and community levels Participates in course and programmatic assessment activities Participates in community and professional activities Participates in student recruitment and retention activities Advises currently enrolled and perspective students Scholarship: Maintains appropriate scholarly and professional development activities Provides expertise in the area of medical-surgical nursing Leadership: Contributes to the continuing innovation and development of the programs in the School of Nursing Participates in the assessment, evaluation, and accreditation of the School of Nursing programs and the University Participates in, manage, or lead projects within the School of Nursing, and University as requested Performs related duties as necessary and as assigned. Minimum Required Education Masters of Science in Nursing (required or near completion) Doctoral degree in nursing preferred Required Licenses and/or Certifications Unencumbered license as a Registered Professional Nurse in WV Required Licenses Certs Summary Unencumbered license as a Registered Professional Nurse in WV Minimum Required Qualifications - Minimum of two (2) years recent acute care experience with a focus in medical-surgical nursing, ICU , mental health, e.g. - Proficiency with Microsoft Office Required Quals Summary - Minimum of two (2) years recent acute care experience with a focus in medical-surgical nursing, ICU , mental health, e.g. - Proficiency with Microsoft Office Preferred Qualifications - Doctorate degree - Previous teaching experience in the classroom, skills and simulation lab - Experience with assessment and national accreditation - Ability to work in a collaborative environment - Familiarity with Blackboard Learning Management System - Familiarity with on-line learning - Ability to foster student learning through innovative teaching modalities - Ability to develop and maintain partnerships within the University, clinical agencies and profession - Commitment to the University and School of Nursing mission Posting Detail Information Requisition Number 2026048FP Number of Vacancies 1 Anticipated Hire Date ASAP Position End Date (if temporary) Job Open Date 08/11/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Applicant Instructions Advertising Summary Quicklink for Posting https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11675 Job Duties Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Optional Documents Certification/License Transcript #1 Transcript #2 Transcript #3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Contact Us For questions relating to Faculty/Staff positions, please e-mail the Human Resources Office at HR@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4111. For questions relating to Student Employment, please e-mail the Student Employment Office at studentjobs@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4836. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11935": {"title": "Assistant Vice President of Facilities", "description": "Fairmont State University Portal | Assistant Vice President of Facilities Skip to Main Content Office of Human Resources 1201 Locust Avenue, Fairmont, West Virginia 26554 Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Vice President of Facilities Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Summary Working Title Assistant Vice President of Facilities Type of Position Staff - Full Time Department Facilities - Skilled Crafts Appointment Length July - June (12 mo) Benefits Eligible? Yes Published Salary Requested Part-Time Staff Hours NA F.T.E. 1.00 Grant Funded Position? No If temporary (or grant funded) position, indicate ending date Description of Job Duties and Responsibilities Job Description Summary: The Assistant Vice President for Facilities provides leadership and management oversight for all aspects of facilities, maintenance, grounds, custodial, construction, utilities, labor crews, and infrastructure. This includes the formulation of policy and standards, standards and procedures, safety practices, physical plant assessment, and occupational security standards. The AVP will foster a culture of process improvement and service orientation for the campus; evaluate and prioritize facility initiatives; and collaborate with stakeholders to further institutional strategic and operational goals to ensure the effective, efficient, and secure operation of all facilities. The AVP will be a creative and strategic leader, exhibit outstanding collaboration skills, and be an excellent communicator. The AVP reports to the Vice President of Finance & Administration and Chief Financial Officer. This position has been designated as essential. This means that when Fairmont State University is faced with an institutional emergency, employees in such positions may be required to remain at their work location or to report to work to protect, recover, and continue operations at Fairmont State University. Fairmont State University is an equal-opportunity employer and is committed to enhancing diversity among its faculty and staff. Duties and Responsibilities: The AVP has responsibility for all aspects of the institution\u2019s physical plant, trades and services, custodial, grounds, occupational safety, construction, and deferred maintenance program as well as all related departmental budgets and staff. Specific oversight functions include but are not limited to the following: The AVP of Facilities will integrate into the Universities culture as a collaborative service provider and partner within all levels of the organization. Develop a service and student oriented mentality within the Facilities organization to support the strategic vision of the President and Board of Governors. Plans, sets priorities, identifies measurable outcomes, and oversees all major facilities functions and policies in alignment with the institution\u2019s strategic initiatives. Drives a team environment within the Facilities Department, keeping customer service, student support, and accountability as primary directives. Establish and drive a maintenance and support culture to make all facilities and grounds a place of pride within the University community. Develop a robust preventive maintenance life cycle plan and recommend funding streams for the replacement of campus infrastructure. Facilitates professional training and development of employees; holds subordinates accountable for effectiveness, efficiency, and professional conduct; conducts effective searches by recruiting, hiring, training, evaluating, and motivating employees; participates in the administration of progressive discipline as needed; ensures good performance is rewarded; fosters an environment where all employees feel valued; promotes diversity, equity, and inclusion in all work units and decisions. Coach and ensure team development and training to ensure that best practices are implemented and support a culture of quality customer service. Oversees all capital construction and major deferred maintenance projects including development of RFPs, architectural design reviews, vendor management, quality assurance, system commissioning, invoice authorization, and warranty administration. Provides Directors, Team Leads, and other supervisors with expert technical support and guidance relative to various building systems and equipment; oversees the utilization of the computerized maintenance management system including monthly reporting. Recommends strategic and operational initiatives in support of the Strategic Vision which supports and advances the institution\u2019s priorities. Authorize and oversee the deployment, monitoring, maintenance, development, and support of all facilities-based assets for institution-wide needs. Provide exceptional oversight with multiple vendors, including architects, engineers, and contractors, in coordination with all functional areas under the Facilities program. Supports and helps with the administering of vendor, consultant, and service contracts and ensures that Fairmont State University receives the full scope of service detailed in contracts. Prepare department annual budgets and administer funds according to budget approval. Explore, evaluate, and prioritize opportunities for automation, efficiency, cost reductions, and sustainability efforts. Collaborate with campus leadership in planning for disaster recovery and emergency responses. Maintains awareness of changing trends and regulations that may impact the institution and recommends or take appropriate corrective action as required. Other related duties as assigned. Minimum Required Education Bachelor\u2019s degree in related field required Required Licenses and/or Certifications N/A Minimum Required Qualifications Seven years of senior leadership experience in facilities operations management with a demonstrated history of success in a maintenance organization, campus support, and capital improvement. Preferred candidates will have experience in higher education within the state of West Virginia. Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Advanced knowledge and leadership abilities to move departments in the direction required to achieve the highest standards and support for the Fairmont State University\u2019s faculty, students, and staff. Excellent communication and relationship management. Well-respected and trusted leader with integrity and transparency. Successful leadership experience in higher education. Demonstrated success in implementing and administering policies and processes in compliance with all regulatory requirements. Demonstrates effective budget, contract, and vendor negotiation and management. Demonstrated ability to lead and collaborate with diverse groups of people. Proven ability to work both independently and collaboratively, take initiative in the development and management of concurrent projects, and meet deadlines. Proven ability to maintain a broad organizational perspective and relationship with other departments to effectively carry out the internal and external relationships of the office. Dependability, flexibility, and willingness to oversee, direct, and respond to campus issues or outages during non-standard work schedules. Preferred Qualifications Professional Engineer or Certified Facilities Manager preferred. Posting Detail Information Requisition Number 2027026SP Number of Vacancies 1 Anticipated Hire Date ASAP Position End Date (if temporary) Job Open Date 08/31/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Advertising Summary Quicklink for Posting https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11840 Job Duties Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Optional Documents Certification/License Transcript #1 Transcript #2 Transcript #3 Contact Us For questions relating to Faculty/Staff positions, please e-mail the Human Resources Office at HR@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4111. For questions relating to Student Employment, please e-mail the Student Employment Office at studentjobs@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4836. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11946": {"title": "Fairmont State University Portal", "description": "Fairmont State University Portal | Facilities Design and Construction Manager Skip to Main Content Office of Human Resources 1201 Locust Avenue, Fairmont, West Virginia 26554 Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Facilities Design and Construction Manager Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Summary Working Title Facilities Design and Construction Manager Type of Position Staff - Full Time Department Facilities - Construction and Safety Appointment Length July - June (12 mo) Benefits Eligible? Yes Published Salary Requested Part-Time Staff Hours NA F.T.E. 1.00 Grant Funded Position? No If temporary (or grant funded) position, indicate ending date Description of Job Duties and Responsibilities Knowledgeable in LEED and Green criteria. Technical expertise in all AutoCAD applications, including Revit Architecture, Adobe applications including photoshop and illustrator, ArcGIS, SketchUp6, Microsoft Office, including Microsoft Office Publisher and Microsoft Office Project. Excellent organizational skills for classifying drawings, O&M Manuals, submittals, and other construction documents. Provide various training to physical plant staff and faculty on Fairmont State campus. Assist with Fairmont State\u2019s part with Higher Education Policy Commissions utilization plan, and facilities condition assessments. Revise physical plant management forms as needed and update files online. Serve as hiring manager for architectural interns. Plan, execute, and finalize construction projects according to deadlines and within budget. This includes acquiring resources and coordinating efforts of team members and third-party contractors, architects, and engineering firms in order to deliver projects according to plan. Review project drawings from schematic design, design development, and through construction. Identify and aid in resolving issues and/or conflicts that may arise during construction projects. Plan and schedule project timelines and milestones using appropriate tools. Take part in construction progress meetings for all on-going projects. Track and keep current spreadsheet o RFI ;s, change orders, contingency funds, and pay applications. Manage electronic and hard documents for project portfolios throughout duration of projects. Make as-built changes to drawings, as well as field verify data and drawings. Develop and delivery progress reports and construction updates weekly. Maintain these reports and make available as requested. Design, plan, and estimate smaller construction projects on main campus as well as other sites. Have the capability and training to design and plan smaller construction projects through the campus including: office space build-outs, retaining walls, restrooms, etc. Oversee student worker and facility space change requests. Participate on various committees, providing consultation and advise to help steer and plan for future expansion, planning of campus buildings and infrastructure. Provide budget numbers, assist in capital project plans, and master plans. Aid in the implementation and oversight of the MS4 (Municipal Separate Storm Sewer Systems) NPDES permitting and Storm Water Management Plan ( SWMP ) for campus. Ensure compliance with all DEP and MS4 regulations. Assist with eDMR reporting and annual report to the DEP . Perform other appropriate duties as assigned. Adhere to and comply with all relevant federal, state, and local laws; if assigned a State purchasing card abide by all purchasing rules and provisions and reports/balances account as required or directed; adhere to all institutional policies and guidelines including the provision of the employee\u2019s relevant employee handbook; adhere to and comply with relevant provisions of the WV State Ethics Act; adhere to all safety rules and provisions, report any personal accidents/injuries timely. Minimum Required Education Requires a Bachelor\u2019s Degree in Architecture, Engineering, or Construction Management, plus two to three (2-3) years of directly related experience; or any equivalent combination of experience and training which provides the required knowledge, skills and abilities. Required Licenses and/or Certifications Computer Aided Design ( CAD ) Certificate Minimum Required Qualifications Demonstrated in-depth knowledge of the construction management process to include appropriate planning, design, coordination, estimating, material and installation specifications, material procurement, scheduling, budgeting, and project coordination. Demonstrated ability to prepare estimates by Construction Division Indexes (i.e. HVAC , electrical, plumbing, etc.) Demonstrated ability to understand blueprints and to review, interpret, and apply project drawings from schematic design through construction implementation. Demonstrated ability to prepare design sketches and interpret construction drawings, Preferred Qualifications NA Posting Detail Information Requisition Number 2027030SP Number of Vacancies 1 Anticipated Hire Date ASAP Position End Date (if temporary) Job Open Date 09/17/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Advertising Summary Quicklink for Posting https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11944 Job Duties Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Optional Documents Certification/License Transcript #1 Transcript #2 Transcript #3 Contact Us For questions relating to Faculty/Staff positions, please e-mail the Human Resources Office at HR@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4111. For questions relating to Student Employment, please e-mail the Student Employment Office at studentjobs@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4836. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11943": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Nursing", "description": "Fairmont State University Portal | Assistant Professor of Nursing Skip to Main Content Office of Human Resources 1201 Locust Avenue, Fairmont, West Virginia 26554 Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor of Nursing Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Summary Working Title Assistant Professor of Nursing Type of Position Faculty Department College of Nursing Appointment Length Aug - May (9 mo) Tenure Status 2 - Tenure Track Academic Rank 3 - Assistant Professor Is this considered a \"term\" position? No Benefits Eligible? Yes Published Salary F.T.E. 1.00 Grant Funded Position? No If temporary (or grant funded) position, indicate ending date Description of Job Duties and Responsibilities Teaching: Participates in the development and evaluation of the ASN and/or BSN program Develops, teaches, and evaluates assigned courses Evaluates student performance on exams and course assignments Evaluates student performance in the clinical environment; including skills lab and simulation lab Assumes responsibility for serving as a course coordinator, as appropriate Coordinates clinical rotation with clinical agency and clinical adjuncts Teaches 12 credits per semester, includes theory, clinical, skills lab and simulation lab Participate in ongoing course and curriculum revision Service: Provides engaged service at the programmatic, School, University and community levels Participates in course and programmatic assessment activities Participates in community and professional activities Participates in student recruitment and retention activities Advises currently enrolled and perspective students Scholarship: Maintains appropriate scholarly and professional development activities Provides expertise in the area of medical-surgical nursing Leadership: Contributes to the continuing innovation and development of the programs in the School of Nursing Participates in the assessment, evaluation, and accreditation of the School of Nursing programs and the University Participates in, manage, or lead projects within the School of Nursing, and University as requested Performs related duties as necessary and as assigned. Minimum Required Education Masters of Science in Nursing (required or near completion) Doctoral degree in nursing preferred Minimum of two (2) years recent experience in academic nursing education Required Licenses and/or Certifications Unencumbered license as a Registered Professional Nurse in WV Required Licenses Certs Summary Unencumbered license as a Registered Professional Nurse in WV Minimum Required Qualifications Masters of Science in Nursing (required or near completion) Doctoral degree in nursing preferred Required Quals Summary Masters of Science in Nursing (required or near completion) Doctoral degree in nursing preferred Preferred Qualifications NA Posting Detail Information Requisition Number 2026047FP Number of Vacancies 1 Anticipated Hire Date ASAP Position End Date (if temporary) Job Open Date 08/11/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Applicant Instructions Advertising Summary Quicklink for Posting https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11671 Job Duties Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Optional Documents Certification/License Transcript #1 Transcript #2 Transcript #3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Contact Us For questions relating to Faculty/Staff positions, please e-mail the Human Resources Office at HR@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4111. For questions relating to Student Employment, please e-mail the Student Employment Office at studentjobs@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4836. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11976": {"title": "Enrollment Systems Specialist", "description": "Fairmont State University Portal | Enrollment Systems Specialist Skip to Main Content Office of Human Resources 1201 Locust Avenue, Fairmont, West Virginia 26554 Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Enrollment Systems Specialist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Summary Working Title Enrollment Systems Specialist Type of Position Staff - Full Time Department Enrollment Services Appointment Length July - June (12 mo) Benefits Eligible? Yes Published Salary Requested Part-Time Staff Hours NA F.T.E. 1.00 Grant Funded Position? No If temporary (or grant funded) position, indicate ending date Description of Job Duties and Responsibilities Reporting to the Director of Enrollment Technology and Operations, the Enrollment Systems Specialist will be an expert in the use and optimization of the Slate CRM and related systems to support the successful business operations of the Enrollment Management division and the mission and goals of the University. This position is required to work on campus a minimum of four days per week. The remaining workday may be completed remotely, subject to departmental needs and supervisor approval. Duties and Responsibilities: Configure, maintain, and troubleshoot enrollment management CRM software. Ensure CRM data integrity by implementing and requiring data standards and uniformity. Ensure adherence to federal and institutional data privacy regulations and policies. Perform daily de-duplication and cleansing of CRM person and organization data. Manage CRM end-users to include development of roles and permissions that follows industry best practices for minimum amount of access to support successful completion of job duties. Be an enrollment management data expert to support accurate creation and maintenance of CRM data queries and reports. Ensure alignment of data collection and categorization across the CRM and student information system. Evaluate current and future Enrollment Management business process operations needs and identify how the CRM can be used to provide the most optimal and productive operational outcomes. Recommend and implement business process workflows. Provide daily operational support to Slate end-users via service management software to include triaging and resolution of issues. Partner with central IT teams to build and maintain data interfaces between Slate and other University systems as well as with external partners. Perform data uploads, monitor automations, and manage error handling. Document all aspects of the CRM related to system administration and data interfacing. Create and maintain knowledge base articles related to the functional use of the CRM . Collaborate with and support departments like Admissions, Financial Aid, IT, and the academic colleges and schools in the effective use of the CRM to improve business strategies and attain enrollment goals. Utilize programming languages like SQL , HTML , CSS , and JavaScript for system customization. Other duties as assigned. Minimum Required Education Bachelor\u2019s Degree. Required Licenses and/or Certifications Valid Driver\u2019s License. Minimum Required Qualifications Experience in administering technology in a higher education setting. Knowledge of higher education policy and practices. Experience administering and utilizing CRM software. Experience managing database records and ensuring data integrity to include compliance with data privacy policies. Preferred Qualifications Experience with Slate Technolutions CRM Software Posting Detail Information Requisition Number 2027020SP Number of Vacancies 1 Anticipated Hire Date ASAP Position End Date (if temporary) Job Open Date 08/21/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Advertising Summary Quicklink for Posting https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11785 Job Duties Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Optional Documents Certification/License Transcript #1 Transcript #2 Transcript #3 Contact Us For questions relating to Faculty/Staff positions, please e-mail the Human Resources Office at HR@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4111. For questions relating to Student Employment, please e-mail the Student Employment Office at studentjobs@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4836. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/12002": {"title": "Fairmont State University Portal", "description": "Fairmont State University Portal | Dean of the College of Business &amp; Aviation Skip to Main Content Office of Human Resources 1201 Locust Avenue, Fairmont, West Virginia 26554 Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Dean of the College of Business & Aviation Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | This posting does not accept online applications. Please contact your Human Resource Office for instructions on how to apply. Posting Details Posting Summary Working Title Dean of the College of Business & Aviation Type of Position Faculty Department College of Business & Aviation Appointment Length July - June (12 mo) Tenure Status 2 - Tenure Track Academic Rank 2 - Associate Professor Is this considered a \"term\" position? No Benefits Eligible? Yes Published Salary F.T.E. 1.00 Grant Funded Position? No If temporary (or grant funded) position, indicate ending date Description of Job Duties and Responsibilities Fairmont State University, a public comprehensive university in vibrant North Central West Virginia, invites inquiries, applications, and nominations for Dean of the College of Business and Aviation ( COBA ). The new Dean is expected to take office in July 2027 . The position is a full-time, 12-month administrative appointment with tenure-track faculty rank eligibility in year three. The anticipated salary is $150,000 \u2013 $175,000. Reporting to the Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs, the Dean is the chief academic and administrative officer of the College and an intellectual leader for both the College and the University, fostering excellence in teaching, research, and service. The role carries full responsibility for the academic leadership, strategic planning, and budgetary and administrative management of the College\u2019s educational, academic support, and ancillary programs. Academic Search is partnering with Fairmont State University on this search, led by Dr. Pam Balch, Senior Consultant. For more information about the position, institution, College, leadership agenda, qualifications, and online application instructions, please review the position profile on the Academic Search website: https://www.academicsearch.org/open-searches-public /. All inquiries, applications, and nominations will be held in confidence. Candidates who would like to learn more may send a CV to FairmontStateDeanCOBA@academicsearch.org to schedule a confidential conversation. Although the position is open until filled, candidates are encouraged to submit all materials by Sunday, November 8, 2026, for full consideration. Leaders who know outstanding candidates are encouraged to submit confidential nominations by sending the nominee\u2019s full name, current position, institution or organization, and email address to FairmontStateDeanCOBA@academicsearch.org . Fairmont State University does not discriminate against employees, students, or applicants on the basis of race, color, gender, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression/association, national origin, age, height, weight, religion, creed, genetic information, disability, or veteran\u2019s status, as identified and defined by law in employment, admissions, and educational programs and activities. Minorities/Women/Veterans/those with disabilities are encouraged to apply. Fairmont State University will not discharge or in any other manner discriminate against any employee or applicant for employment because such employee or applicant has inquired about, discussed, or disclosed the compensation of the employee or applicant or another employee or applicant. Position Summary: Fairmont State University, a public comprehensive university in vibrant North-Central West Virginia, invites inquiries, applications, and nominations for Dean of the College of Business and Aviation ( COBA ). The new Dean is expected to take office in July 2027. Founded as a normal school in 1865\u201367, Fairmont State became a State Teachers College in 1931, Fairmont State College in 1944, and Fairmont State University in 2004. Its motto is \u201cScholarship, Opportunity, Achievement, and Responsibility.\u201d The University is a comprehensive, student-centered, state supported institution offering 56 certificates and degrees at the associate, bachelor\u2019s, and master\u2019s levels. On a hilltop campus in Fairmont, West Virginia, Fairmont State combines the opportunities of a large public university with the personal attention of a smaller private institution. Fairmont State\u2019s 120-acre campus includes more than 20 buildings. Recent decades have brought a new student union, parking garage, and residence hall, along with major infrastructure improvements to campus accessibility. The University also operates the Robert C. Byrd National Aerospace Education Center in Bridgeport, West Virginia. The university enrolls about 3,300 students in its undergraduate and graduate programs. Reporting to the Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs, the Dean is the chief academic and administrative officer of the College and an intellectual leader for both the College and the University, fostering excellence in teaching, research, and service. The role carries full responsibility for the academic leadership, strategic planning, and budgetary and administrative management of the College\u2019s educational, academic support, and ancillary programs. The Dean also leads every dimension of the College\u2019s external engagement\u2014development, fundraising, alumni relations, partnerships with outside organizations, and the College\u2019s reputation across the state and region. Success calls for the strategic vision to identify and pursue new opportunities and the intellectual strength to guide the College\u2019s growth within the framework of shared academic governance and the University\u2019s mission. The position is a full-time, 12-month administrative appointment with tenure-track faculty rank eligibility in year three. The anticipated salary is $150,000 \u2013 $175,000. Leadership Priorities LEAD THE COLLEGE IN STRATEGIC PLANNING AND ACCOUNTABILITY Provide academic leadership and strategic planning for the College\u2019s educational, academic support, and ancillary programs. Guide the faculty in developing a college strategic plan aligned with the Academic Implementation Plan and the University\u2019s Strategic Vision 2025-2035. With the COBA leadership team and faculty, establish a sustainable process for reporting progress toward strategic objectives and key performance indicators. ADMINISTER THE COLLEGE\u2019S ACADEMIC PROGRAMS AND OPERATIONS Administer the College\u2019s academic programs: supervise administrative and support staff, oversee the three department chairs, manage resources, conduct department and institution-wide assessments, promote faculty development, and support student advising, recruitment, and retention. Provide day-to-day budgetary and administrative management that allows faculty to teach well and students to progress. STRENGTHEN ASSESSMENT AND ACCREDITATION READINESS With the College\u2019s Director of Assessment and the University\u2019s Assurance of Learning Director, evaluate and strengthen assessment practices, student learning outcomes, and reporting processes. Use data-informed decision making and rigorous program evaluation to ensure curricula and operations continue to meet the standards of institutional, state, regional, and specialized accrediting bodies, including ACBSP . GROW ENROLLMENT AND ADVANCE STUDENT SUCCESS Lead enrollment management initiatives\u2014student recruitment, admission, progression, retention, and completion\u2014in collaboration with other University divisions. Build an environment that prioritizes student learning, career readiness and engagement, and expand opportunities for contextualized learning, internships, and work-based experiences. AMPLIFY THE STUDENT VOICE Reestablish a student advisory council that gives students meaningful input on the College\u2019s priorities, curricula, cocurricular programming, and overall experience. EXPAND CERTIFICATIONS AND MICROCREDENTIALS Extend industry-recognized certifications and microcredentials for faculty and students well beyond their current use, tightening the connection between the classroom and the careers students are preparing to enter. DEEPEN PARTNERSHIPS WITH BUSINESS , INDUSTRY , AND GOVERNMENT Build on established relationships with partners such as Leidos, Trilogy, The Rodeheaver Group, Baker Tilly, MVA Health Centers and the FBI to expand internships and work-based learning, promote entrepreneurship, strengthen program advisory board participation, and cultivate new partners across the I-79 High Tech Corridor, the region\u2019s aviation sector, and the healthcare and financial services employers who hire COBA graduates. Sustain the business and industry linkages that make contextualized learning possible in every discipline in the College. ADVANCE EXTERNAL ENGAGEMENT AND RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT Lead the College\u2019s development, fundraising, alumni relations, and grant-seeking. Pursue external grants and private funding for new projects and ongoing initiatives, support faculty in securing external funding for research and scholarly activity, and raise the College\u2019s visibility and reputation across West Virginia and the broader region. STEWARD RESOURCES WITH CLEAR PRIORITIES Review budget priorities and goals so that resources support teaching, learning, and student engagement are sustained. Manage the College\u2019s budget and administrative operations transparently, with a clear rationale for decisions. RECRUIT , DEVELOP , AND RETAIN OUTSTANDING FACULTY AND STAFF Recruit, mentor, evaluate, and retain professionally and academically qualified faculty and staff to support teaching, professional development, advising, service, and scholarship. Foster a culture of collaboration among faculty and department chairs, invest in faculty development, and advocate for new approaches to teaching and learning, particularly those enabled by current and emerging technologies. LEAD COLLABORATIVELY ACROSS THE UNIVERSITY Lead collaboratively through consultative decision making, information sharing, and consensus building with COBA stakeholders, fellow Deans, the Office of the Provost, and senior University leadership, and participate actively in university administrative groups and committees. Minimum Required Education An earned doctorate and professional background in a relevant discipline within the College. Required Licenses and/or Certifications NA Required Licenses Certs Summary NA Minimum Required Qualifications Candidates should demonstrate a strong commitment toteaching excellence and service consistent with the missionof the College and the University, evidence of creativeand effective teaching in accredited institutions of highereducation, and experience in online course development anddistance education. Experience: Progressively responsible academic leadership experience, preferably at the level of department chair or higher. Academic Record: A distinguished record of teaching, scholarship, and service that merits a tenured appointment at the rank of associate or full professor. Accreditation: Demonstrated experience with collegiate business school accreditation processes ( ACBSP , AACSB ). Required Quals Summary Candidates should demonstrate a strong commitment toteaching excellence and service consistent with the missionof the College and the University, evidence of creativeand effective teaching in accredited institutions of highereducation, and experience in online course development anddistance education. Experience: Progressively responsible academic leadership experience, preferably at the level of department chair or higher. Academic Record: A distinguished record of teaching, scholarship, and service that merits a tenured appointment at the rank of associate or full professor. Accreditation: Demonstrated experience with collegiate business school accreditation processes ( ACBSP , AACSB ). Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated success in inspiring others toward shared goals with integrity and fairness. Familiarity with current higher education policy and trends, particularly regional and specialized accreditation standards. Experience managing complex budgets and supervising personnel. Skill in strategic planning and resource management. Record of fostering a culture of opportunity that values diverse views and perspectives and enables students, faculty, and staff to succeed. Experience with faculty appointments, fundraising, grantsmanship, and community outreach. Posting Detail Information Requisition Number 2026052FP Number of Vacancies 1 Anticipated Hire Date July 2027 Position End Date (if temporary) Job Open Date 09/30/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Applicant Instructions Advertising Summary Quicklink for Posting https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/12000 Job Duties Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Contact Us For questions relating to Faculty/Staff positions, please e-mail the Human Resources Office at HR@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4111. For questions relating to Student Employment, please e-mail the Student Employment Office at studentjobs@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4836. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/12030": {"title": "Assistant Director of Student Success", "description": "Fairmont State University Portal | Assistant Director of Student Success Skip to Main Content Office of Human Resources 1201 Locust Avenue, Fairmont, West Virginia 26554 Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Director of Student Success Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Summary Working Title Assistant Director of Student Success Type of Position Staff - Full Time Department Student Success Appointment Length July - June (12 mo) Benefits Eligible? Yes Published Salary Requested Part-Time Staff Hours NA F.T.E. 1.00 Grant Funded Position? No If temporary (or grant funded) position, indicate ending date Description of Job Duties and Responsibilities Position Summary The Assistant Director of Student Success serves as an operational leader for the Student Success team within Enrollment Management and provides oversight for daily coordination, implementation, and assessment of student success initiatives, student support services, and retention-related operations. At the direction of the Director of Student Success this position provides supervision and leadership to a team of Student Success Specialists while serving as a primary operational liaison between Enrollment Management, Student Affairs, Athletics, Academic Affairs, and other campus partners to ensure students receive coordinated, proactive, and student-centered support throughout their educational journey. The Assistant Director is responsible for managing day-to-day student success operations, coordinating student intervention efforts, monitoring outreach and engagement initiatives, overseeing student support workflows, and assisting with institutional retention efforts using data, technology platforms, and collaborative strategies. This position plays a key role in supporting institutional enrollment, persistence, retention, and student success goals while ensuring operational consistency, accountability, and high-quality student service delivery. The Director of Student Success may alter duties and responsibilities as necessary. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Student Success Operations & Leadership \u2022 Oversee the daily operations of the Student Success area within Enrollment Management. \u2022 Coordinate and manage frontline student support operations and service delivery within the Turley Center. \u2022 Ensure students receive prompt, accurate, and student-centered support related to enrollment, financial aid, student accounts, housing, registration, retention, and student success services. \u2022 Assist in the implementation and execution of institutional retention and persistence initiatives. \u2022 Monitor operational effectiveness and identify opportunities for process improvement and enhanced student support. \u2022 Assist with development and implementation of operational procedures, communication workflows, and student engagement strategies. \u2022 Coordinate student outreach and intervention efforts related to retention, persistence, registration, and student success campaigns. \u2022 Support divisional and institutional enrollment management initiatives as assigned. \u2022 Serve as backup support for safe management and cashiering operations, including opening and closing sessions, balancing daily receipts, and ensuring funds are secured in accordance with university policies and internal controls. Assist in monitoring compliance with cash handling procedures, maintaining accurate records, and escalating discrepancies as needed. \u2022 Maintain proper documentation of cash transactions and report any discrepancies in accordance with departmental policy. Supervision & Staff Management \u2022 Provide direct supervision, leadership, training, and operational oversight to Student Success Specialists and assigned student employees. \u2022 Coordinate staff schedules, office coverage, and operational workflows to ensure consistent student support and service delivery. \u2022 Conduct onboarding and training for new staff members related to university systems, customer service expectations, operational procedures, and student support protocols. \u2022 Monitor staff performance, productivity, documentation, responsiveness, and adherence to institutional expectations and operational procedures. \u2022 Assist with performance evaluations, coaching, professional development, and corrective action documentation as appropriate. \u2022 Foster a collaborative, student-centered, and solutions-oriented team of culture. Student Support, Outreach & Intervention \u2022 Provide leadership, coordination, and accountability for Student Success Specialists and support staff in advancing institutional retention and persistence goals. \u2022 Ensure Specialists actively contribute toward divisional and university retention objectives through proactive outreach, student engagement, intervention efforts, and coordinated student support initiatives. \u2022 Collaborate with the Director of Student Success to monitor retention progress, identify barriers impacting persistence, and implement operational strategies that support overall student retention and success. \u2022 Coordinate proactive student outreach efforts related to: o Registration o Academic progress o Early alerts o Student account concerns o Financial aid follow-up o Enrollment persistence o Retention campaigns \u2022 Assist the Director in managing student intervention strategies for at-risk students through coordinated support efforts and referrals. \u2022 Serve as an escalation point for complex student concerns requiring other coordination or support. \u2022 Coordinate referrals between Enrollment Management, Student Affairs, Academic Affairs, CARE Team representatives, and other campus resources. \u2022 Assist with orientation, welcome programming, commencement activities, Maroon & White events, and other enrollment and retention-related initiatives. Technology & Reporting \u2022 Lead with operational oversight and utilization of Navigate360/Slate and other student success technologies, serving as a SuperUser representative for the Enrollment Management Division with operational oversight and utilization of Navigate360/Slate and other student success technologies. \u2022 Monitor and ensure appropriate documentation standards and utilization expectations within Navigate360/Slate. \u2022 Provide regular reports to the Director on efficacy of outreach and campaigns and any other pertinent information related to retention. \u2022 Assist with development and execution of student success campaigns, appointment campaigns, early alerts, and retention initiatives within Navigate360/Slate. \u2022 Utilize institutional data, reporting tools, and student success technologies to monitor outreach effectiveness, identify trends, and support operational decision-making. \u2022 Collaborate with Institutional Research, Information Technology, and campus stakeholders to improve student success reporting and intervention processes. Minimum Required Education Minimum of a Bachelor\u2019s Degree in Education, Business Administration, Psychology in a related field. Required Licenses and/or Certifications N/A Minimum Required Qualifications Minimum of three (3) years of progressive experience in student services, enrollment management, student success, retention, advising, or related higher education operations. Demonstrated experience coordinating student support services and managing operational workflows. Experience supervising staff, student employees, or teams. Strong interpersonal, organizational, and communication skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. Experience using student information systems, CRM platforms, or student success technologies. Ability to analyze information, solve problems, and make sound operational decisions. Preferred Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in Higher Education, Student Affairs, Counseling, Leadership, or related field. Experience utilizing Navigate360, Banner, Slate, TouchNet, or related higher education systems. Experience with student retention initiatives, early alert systems, and student intervention models. Experience working collaboratively across academic and student support units. Posting Detail Information Requisition Number 2027015SP Number of Vacancies 1 Anticipated Hire Date ASAP Position End Date (if temporary) Job Open Date 08/19/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Advertising Summary Quicklink for Posting https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11756 Job Duties Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Optional Documents Certification/License Transcript #1 Transcript #2 Transcript #3 Contact Us For questions relating to Faculty/Staff positions, please e-mail the Human Resources Office at HR@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4111. For questions relating to Student Employment, please e-mail the Student Employment Office at studentjobs@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4836. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/12060": {"title": "Events and Facilities Operations Worker", "description": "Fairmont State University Portal | Events and Facilities Operations Worker Skip to Main Content Office of Human Resources 1201 Locust Avenue, Fairmont, West Virginia 26554 Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Events and Facilities Operations Worker Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Summary Working Title Events and Facilities Operations Worker Type of Position Staff - Full Time Department Facilities - Grounds Appointment Length July - June (12 mo) Benefits Eligible? Yes Published Salary Requested Part-Time Staff Hours NA F.T.E. 1.00 Grant Funded Position? No If temporary (or grant funded) position, indicate ending date Description of Job Duties and Responsibilities Fairmont State University is seeking a dependable, safety-conscious, and service-oriented individual to join our Facilities team. This position plays an important role in supporting daily campus operations, university events, and the overall appearance, safety, and functionality of our campus. Performs a variety of hands-on duties, including event setup and breakdown, furniture and equipment relocation, groundskeeping, snow and ice removal, sanitation, material transportation, and general facilities support. The successful candidate will operate a variety of vehicles, tools, and equipment and work collaboratively with university departments to support campus activities and special events. This position requires flexibility, physical stamina, a commitment to safety, and the ability to respond to changing operational needs, including inclement weather and occasional mandatory overtime. If you enjoy working in a team-oriented environment and take pride in helping maintain a welcoming, safe, and well-functioning campus, we encourage you to apply and become part of the Fairmont State University community. Incumbent will support all university events through set-ups, tear downs, loading and moving of needed material and equipment including tables, chairs, tents, benches, etc. Relocates offices and classrooms within buildings and throughout campus by lifting, loading and unloading furniture, filing cabinets, boxes, etc. onto hand trucks, dollies, and box vans for transportation. May require removing desk components, doors, and shelves to ease in relocations. Moves, sets-up, rearranges, and erects tables, chairs, platforms, bleachers, tents, displays, etc. May assist in the design for special event set-ups. Reads floor plans and layouts for concerts, registration, commencement, and other special statewide University affiliated events. Drives box vans, forklifts, front loaders, small dump trucks, and operates lift gates. Operates, maintains, and services equipment and tools that are used while performing moves, set-ups, sanitation services, and snow removal. Operates motor vehicle (i.e. car, box van, pick-up truck, fork lift, front loader, small dump truck\u2026) to transport people, to deliver/receive surplus for inventory control, to deliver, receive, or remove surplus materials for shops and equipment throughout the campus and community and statewide. Unloads and stores supplies, rotating stock and equipment at various job sites. Establishes and maintains inventory of departments throughout institutional buildings, warehouse, or stockroom on equipment e.g. tables, chairs, tents, staging, platforms. Collects and properly disposes of trash and litter throughout institutional buildings and grounds, including cleaning of trash receptacles and assisting sanitation vehicles operators. Collects and properly stores hazardous materials, e.g. muriatic acid, propane, diesel fuel, anti-freeze, chlorine, alcohol, and sodium bi-carbonate. At time of inclement weather or as directed by Facilities administration, will work as required to removes snow from sidewalks, steps, roads, and parking lots using hand tools, power brooms, and snow blowers. Spreads de-icers and limestone chips on all areas as needed. Removes graffiti from walls and sidewalks; performs all outside cleaning activities as required. Operates high-pressure washers, sandblasters, and other power equipment to complete these tasks. Operates blowers and walk-behind sweepers to clean and remove debris in maintaining the appearance of institutional grounds. As assigned, assists with landscape construction by: operating jackhammers and other related equipment to remove broken sidewalks; mixing, pouring, and spreading concrete, asphalt, gravel, and other materials; digs holes and trenches to assist in the repair or replacement of utility lines, irrigation and drainage systems by using hand and power tools; excavates and prepares grounds prior to initiation of construction projects. As needed, will be required to maintain and care for institutional grounds by mowing, trimming and edging around trees, flower beds, buildings, and walkways; watering lawns, shrubs, and ornamental gardens during dry periods. Removes weeds from flowers, shrubs, and ground cover as required. Removing and disposing of debris throughout grounds area. Collects recyclable items and places in appropriate storage location. Must be able to provide support to academics, special events for Fairmont State University campus community and throughout the state, which requires flexible hours and mandatory overtime. As needed, assists in preparing grounds and ornamental beds for planting and seeding, hauls and spreads topsoil and mixed in fertilizer, peat moss, compost vermiculite, and other additives to condition the soil. Assists in planting ornamentals, flowers, shrubs, and trees as required. As needed, operates, services, and maintains hand power tools and equipment such as weed-eaters, lawn mowers, roto-tillers, walk-behind sweepers, and vacs. Positions are considered essential and should plan to work during inclement weather or snow events. Positions could be assigned to work non-standard hours as required. May be required to perform various maintenance tasks either assisting or under the direction of qualified craft persons (plumbing, carpentry, painting, etc.). These tasks would be considered non-technical, non-certified, supporting duties. Attends various training classes, seminars, and other meetings to learn new techniques and procedures and to remain current in all safety requirements. Must be able to respond to emergency situations and events, which include snow removal. Minimum Required Education High School Diploma or GED Required Licenses and/or Certifications West Virginia Driver\u2019s License Minimum Required Qualifications Ability to perform physically demanding outdoor work in various weather conditions. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Strong work ethic and reliability. Knowledge of landscaping practices and grounds maintenance. Ability to lift up to 50 pounds and perform repetitive physical tasks. Good communication skills. Preferred Qualifications Ability and capability to perform essential job functions. Posting Detail Information Requisition Number 2027034SP Number of Vacancies 3 Anticipated Hire Date ASAP Position End Date (if temporary) Job Open Date 10/21/2026 Job Close Date 11/04/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Advertising Summary Quicklink for Posting https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/12058 Job Duties Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Optional Documents Certification/License Transcript #1 Transcript #2 Transcript #3 Contact Us For questions relating to Faculty/Staff positions, please e-mail the Human Resources Office at HR@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4111. For questions relating to Student Employment, please e-mail the Student Employment Office at studentjobs@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4836. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/12028": {"title": "Financial Reporting Manager", "description": "Fairmont State University Portal | Financial Reporting Manager Skip to Main Content Office of Human Resources 1201 Locust Avenue, Fairmont, West Virginia 26554 Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Financial Reporting Manager Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Summary Working Title Financial Reporting Manager Type of Position Staff - Full Time Department Accounting Appointment Length July - June (12 mo) Benefits Eligible? Yes Published Salary Requested Part-Time Staff Hours NA F.T.E. 1.00 Grant Funded Position? No If temporary (or grant funded) position, indicate ending date Description of Job Duties and Responsibilities The Financial Reporting Manager supports the financial operations of Fairmont State University by collecting, reviewing and analyzing financial data for external and internal financial reporting requirements. This role assists in producing timely, accurate and compliant financial reports while adhering to federal, state and institutional regulations and guidelines, maintains strong communication and relationships with the campus community and key financial stakeholders. Operational Duties: Internal Reporting \u2013 Assist with monthly, quarterly and year-end closing activities, including but not limited to preparing accrual entries, completing, reviewing and correcting journal entries, account reconciliations, and financial data to ensure the accuracy of financial information Collect interim financial data, identify significant variances, interpret data, and collaborate with the Finance team to compile monthly financial statements Create regular, recurring and ad hoc internal reports as needed to support university-wide decision-making Internal reporting includes but is not limited to financial statements, capital project budget reports, fixed asset reports and proformas External Reporting \u2013 Collaborate with Institutional Resources to complete all required and requested external reporting in compliance with state, federal and higher education reporting requirements for various third-party stakeholders External reporting includes but is not limited to Internal Revenue Service ( IRS ), National Collegiate Athletic Association ( NCAA ), Integrated Postsecondary Education Data System ( IPEDS ), Higher Education Policy Commission ( HEPC ) and the State of West Virginia. Audit Coordination \u2013 Assist Finance leaders with the preparation of the University\u2019s annual audited consolidated financial statements, ensuring accuracy and compliance with policies, federal and state laws, Generally Accepted Accounting Principles ( GAAP ) and Governmental Accounting Standards Board ( GASB ) standards. Duties include but are not limited to developing workpapers, preparing schedules, creating and reviewing journal entries and collecting documentation. Audits include but are not limited to National Collegiate Athletic Association ( NCAA ), Research & Development (R&D) and Single Financial Audit ( SFA ) Process Improvement & Systems Optimization: Policy Development: Work with Finance team to evaluate, update, implement and document departmental and university-wide financial policies and procedures. Unit Collaboration: Collaboration includes but is not limited to, partnering with the Finance Team to ensure accurate and timely financial reporting and to ensure alignment between budget and actual reporting; and collaborating with departments across the university to promote clear understanding of financial data and processes Improvement: Drive continuous improvement by automating manual processes and enhancing ERP system functionality in conjunction with the State of WV\u2019s ERP system Other: Participates in other projects and performs other duties as assigned. Minimum Required Education Bachelor\u2019s degree in Accounting, Finance, Business Administration or a related business field (or equivalent combination of education and experience). Required Licenses and/or Certifications N/A Minimum Required Qualifications 3-5 years prior experience with Finance, Accounting or Budgets, however, any equivalent combination of education and/or experience is acceptable which provides an applicant with the listed knowledge, skills, abilities and capability to perform the essential functions of the job High attention to detail and strong written and verbal communication skills Strong proficiency in Microsoft Excel (including formulas, data sorting, and pivot tables). Strict ethical standards for handling data confidentiality Preferred Qualifications Experience with higher education finances Experience with annual audit coordination Strong understanding of Generally Accepted Accounting Principles ( GAAP ) and Governmental Accounting Standard Board ( GASB ) Posting Detail Information Requisition Number 2027017SP Number of Vacancies 1 Anticipated Hire Date ASAP Position End Date (if temporary) Job Open Date 08/20/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Advertising Summary Quicklink for Posting https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11768 Job Duties Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Optional Documents Certification/License Transcript #1 Transcript #2 Transcript #3 Contact Us For questions relating to Faculty/Staff positions, please e-mail the Human Resources Office at HR@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4111. For questions relating to Student Employment, please e-mail the Student Employment Office at studentjobs@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4836. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/12038": {"title": "Executive Assistant and Project Manager\u2013 Enrollment Management", "description": "Fairmont State University Portal | Executive Assistant and Project Manager\u2013 Enrollment Management Skip to Main Content Office of Human Resources 1201 Locust Avenue, Fairmont, West Virginia 26554 Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Executive Assistant and Project Manager\u2013 Enrollment Management Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Summary Working Title Executive Assistant and Project Manager\u2013 Enrollment Management Type of Position Staff - Full Time Department Enrollment Management Appointment Length July - June (12 mo) Benefits Eligible? Yes Published Salary Requested Part-Time Staff Hours NA F.T.E. 1.00 Grant Funded Position? No If temporary (or grant funded) position, indicate ending date Description of Job Duties and Responsibilities The Executive Assistant and Project Manager, provides high-level executive, financial, operational, and project management support to the Vice President of Enrollment Management and the Enrollment Management leadership team. Serving as a key operational partner within the division, this position coordinates strategic initiatives, manages divisional projects and timelines, supports budget planning and financial operations, and helps ensure priorities move effectively from planning through implementation. The position works collaboratively across Enrollment Management and with University partners to coordinate complex and cross-functional projects, establish timelines and deliverables, monitor progress, identify barriers, facilitate communication, and provide regular updates to leadership. The position also manages and coordinates divisional budget and procurement activities, executive scheduling for the VP and AVP , communications, travel, personnel processes, and other administrative operations. The successful candidate must demonstrate strong judgment, initiative, organization, discretion, problem-solving skills, and the ability to independently manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Executive and Leadership Support Provide high-level executive and administrative support to the Vice President of Enrollment Management and support the Enrollment Management leadership team as appropriate. Manage the Vice President\u2019s calendar, meetings, appointments, priorities, and scheduling needs. Coordinate meeting logistics, develop agendas and materials, document decisions and action items, and monitor necessary follow-up. Prepare and edit executive correspondence, reports, presentations, briefing materials, and other communications. Coordinate travel arrangements, itineraries, registrations, and related logistics for the Vice President and Enrollment Management leadership as assigned. Serve as a primary point of coordination between the Office of the Vice President, Enrollment Management departments, University leadership, campus partners, and external stakeholders. Exercise discretion and sound judgment when managing confidential, sensitive, or time-critical information. Anticipate needs, identify issues requiring attention, gather necessary information, and assist in developing solutions before matters are escalated to the Vice President. Assist with divisional personnel processes, including full-time hires, temporary appointments, graduate assistants, onboarding, and related administrative needs. Provide coordination and administrative support for Enrollment Management leadership meetings, retreats, planning sessions, and other divisional activities. Budget, Finance, and Procurement Coordinate divisional budget development and ongoing budget management in collaboration with the Vice President, Enrollment Management leadership, Finance, and departmental budget managers. Maintain comprehensive oversight of Enrollment Management budgets, expenditures, commitments, and available resources and provide regular financial updates to leadership. Monitor spending and identify potential budget concerns, resource needs, efficiencies, and opportunities for strategic reallocation. Coordinate regular budget reviews with departmental budget managers to evaluate expenditures, projections, priorities, and resource needs. Manage divisional procurement processes and ensure compliance with University purchasing and financial policies. Coordinate requisitions, purchase orders, vendor documentation, payment processing, purchasing-card activity, and other procurement functions as assigned. Serve as a resource to Enrollment Management staff regarding purchasing, travel, reimbursement, and other divisional financial processes. Coordinate expense reporting and reimbursement processes for designated Enrollment Management employees. Maintain appropriate financial documentation and support reconciliation, reporting, audit, and year-end processes. Collaborate with Finance and Procurement to resolve financial or purchasing issues affecting divisional operations. Project Management and Strategic Initiatives Manage and coordinate strategic projects and initiatives on behalf of the Vice President and Enrollment Management leadership team from initiation through completion. Develop project plans identifying objectives, scope, deliverables, milestones, timelines, responsible parties, dependencies, and anticipated outcomes. Maintain a centralized portfolio of Enrollment Management projects and priorities to provide leadership with visibility into project status, deadlines, outstanding decisions, risks, and next steps. Facilitate cross-functional project meetings and ensure decisions, responsibilities, action items, and deadlines are clearly documented and communicated. Monitor project progress and proactively follow up with responsible individuals and teams to support timely completion of deliverables. Identify project delays, barriers, competing priorities, dependencies, or resource needs and elevate issues requiring leadership attention. Coordinate initiatives involving multiple Enrollment Management units and University partners, establishing clear ownership and facilitating communication across functional areas. Develop and maintain project dashboards, trackers, implementation plans, status reports, executive summaries, presentations, and other project-management tools. Assist leadership with post-project assessment to identify outcomes, lessons learned, unresolved items, and opportunities for continuous improvement. Divisional Operations and Communication Help coordinate operational priorities across Enrollment Management and facilitate communication among divisional departments. Maintain divisional calendars, deadlines, planning documents, project trackers, and other tools that support effective coordination and accountability. Assist with preparing and distributing divisional communications, meeting materials, announcements, reports, and presentations. Coordinate information and materials needed for University leadership, institutional committees, meetings, presentations, and other strategic activities. Establish and maintain organized records and documentation for divisional projects, financial operations, contracts, personnel activities, and administrative processes. Evaluate administrative processes and recommend improvements that increase efficiency, consistency, transparency, and service. Support a collaborative, responsive, student-centered culture throughout Enrollment Management. Perform other duties and coordinate special initiatives as assigned by the Vice President or his/her leadership team. Minimum Required Education Bachelor\u2019s degree or an equivalent combination of education and relevant professional experience. Required Licenses and/or Certifications N/A Minimum Required Qualifications Demonstrated experience managing multiple projects, priorities, and deadlines simultaneously. Strong organizational and project coordination skills with demonstrated attention to detail. Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Demonstrated ability to work independently, exercise sound judgment, solve problems, and appropriately escalate issues. Experience coordinating work involving multiple departments, stakeholders, or functional areas. Ability to develop and maintain project plans, trackers, timelines, reports, and other organizational tools. Demonstrated ability to work effectively with senior leaders and diverse internal and external stakeholders. Ability to handle confidential and sensitive information with discretion. Strong proficiency with Microsoft Office and contemporary collaboration, communication, and productivity technologies. Ability to adapt to changing priorities and operate effectively in a fast-paced environment. Commitment to excellent service and a student-centered University environment. Preferred Qualifications Professional experience in higher education, Enrollment Management, executive administration, business operations, project management, or a related environment. Experience managing or coordinating budgets, procurement, purchasing, or financial operations. Experience coordinating cross-functional projects from planning through implementation. Experience with project-management or collaborative work-management platforms. Experience supporting senior or executive-level leadership. Experience with process improvement, change management, implementation planning, or organizational operations. Project management training or certification. Familiarity with higher education administrative systems, enterprise systems, CRM platforms, or related technology. Posting Detail Information Requisition Number 2027032SP Number of Vacancies 1 Anticipated Hire Date ASAP Position End Date (if temporary) Job Open Date 09/21/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Advertising Summary Quicklink for Posting https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11966 Job Duties Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Optional Documents Certification/License Transcript #1 Transcript #2 Transcript #3 Contact Us For questions relating to Faculty/Staff positions, please e-mail the Human Resources Office at HR@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4111. For questions relating to Student Employment, please e-mail the Student Employment Office at studentjobs@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4836. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/12065": {"title": "Director of the Folklife Center", "description": "Fairmont State University Portal | Director of the Folklife Center Skip to Main Content Office of Human Resources 1201 Locust Avenue, Fairmont, West Virginia 26554 Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Director of the Folklife Center Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Summary Working Title Director of the Folklife Center Type of Position Staff - Full Time Department Community Programs Appointment Length July - June (12 mo) Benefits Eligible? Yes Published Salary Requested Part-Time Staff Hours NA F.T.E. 1.00 Grant Funded Position? No If temporary (or grant funded) position, indicate ending date Description of Job Duties and Responsibilities The Director of the Folklife Center provides leadership and oversight for the development, coordination, and delivery of folk and traditional arts programming that celebrates and preserves West Virginia\u2019s cultural heritage. This position oversees the Center\u2019s exhibitions, collections, archives, publications, and educational programming while fostering meaningful partnerships with community members, cultural organizations, university departments, and external stakeholders. The Director is responsible for the Center\u2019s daily operations, staff supervision, budget management, fundraising initiatives, and stewardship of its facilities and collections, ensuring that the Center advances its mission through community engagement, scholarship, preservation, and public programming. Duties and Responsibilities: Develops and offers folk and traditional arts programming in collaboration with community members and groups Coordinates and directs the work of student workers and staff in the completion of special projects for the Center\u2019s programming; Oversees curation, creation and installation of changing exhibitions and displays; updates permanent displays as needed; Coordinates with staff to oversee archival research and scholarly inquiries; Writes, edits, and publishes related folklife/folklore works on behalf of and for the Center, including press releases, exhibition text, website copy, social media copy, and more; Oversees the publication of Traditions, the annual WV folklore journal; Recommends and manages all protocol and programmatic policies; Oversees budget development and monitoring for the Center and ensures careful stewardship of the Center\u2019s financial and physical assets; Selects, trains, supervises, and evaluates the professional and administrative staff assigned to the Center Collaborates with other university departments and offices to promote programs, exhibitions, and archives; Seeks out opportunities for community collaboration, engagement, and promotion; Collaborates with the College of Liberal Arts, Office of Sponsored Programs, and Fairmont State Foundation on internal and external fundraising, including grants;: In coordination with physical plant, oversees repairs and maintenance of and plans for enhancements to the Center building and grounds; Coordinates with Folklife Center staff, catering, and physical plant on event set-up; Oversees the archiving and curation of the Center\u2019s collections; Oversees proper storage of the Center\u2019s collections; Works with the advisory committee toward creating a quality collection that best embodies the Center\u2019s mission statement; Oversees equipment, supplies, and materials: ensures that equipment is functional and that supplies and materials used in classes, workshops, collections management, exhibitions, and Folklife Center programs are sufficient. Works with other campus stakeholders to coordinate programming and events. Minimum Required Education A Bachelor\u2019s Degree or higher in museum management, history, folklore, or a related field. Required Licenses and/or Certifications N/A Minimum Required Qualifications Demonstrated experience in program development and facilities management. Preferred Qualifications A Master\u2019s Degree or higher in museum management, history, folklore, or a related field. A track record of leadership and experience coordinating and fundraising with local community groups. Posting Detail Information Requisition Number 2027035SP Number of Vacancies 1 Anticipated Hire Date ASAP Position End Date (if temporary) Job Open Date 10/21/2026 Job Close Date 11/04/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Advertising Summary Quicklink for Posting https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/12063 Job Duties Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Optional Documents Certification/License Transcript #1 Transcript #2 Transcript #3 Contact Us For questions relating to Faculty/Staff positions, please e-mail the Human Resources Office at HR@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4111. For questions relating to Student Employment, please e-mail the Student Employment Office at studentjobs@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4836. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}}, "rows": {"https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/8382": {"school_id": 1572, "posting_url": "https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/8382", "job_title_in_post": "Office of Human Resources1201 Locust Avenue, Fairmont, West Virginia 26554", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "Human Resources1201 Locust Avenue, Fairmont, West Virginia 26554", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com